A||N||9||Seanh||Control Arm bolt is pissin me off!||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||06-26-2001||06:07 PM||||Well, 6 hours and 4 wrenchs later, I still don't have the control arm off. Just to let you know the background, I have turned the bolt, and it does turn so it not rusted in the sleeve. I sprayed the hell out of it with oil, but I can't get the damn nut off! I broke a few adjustable wrench's trying to hold the bolt while I turned the nut, I can't seem to find an 18mm wrench in my grage, so I think I'll go in and get one. Got any better ideas how to get the stupid thing off? Maybe just nut splitters if I can't get it off with a wrench?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||06-26-2001||06:24 PM||||Hey Seanh!<BR>Are you sure you got the nut and not the head of the bolt??<BR>Just kiddin!!!<BR>Nut splitter works for me...<BR>Or the blue wrench...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||06-26-2001||09:31 PM||||I finally got that little .....! I got a 1/2" drive ratchet, put a 3ft steel tube over the handle, put an 18mm forged steel wrench on the nut. I put my foot on the wrench, and pulled up on the handle and it finally broke loose. I'm going to go to Advance auto tomarrow and buy all their little packages of anti-sieze that they have. Too much is never enough. Then again, do I really want these to come off again that easialy? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Coop88||06-27-2001||05:58 AM||||You gotta love home-made breaker bars. I use a 6' steel pipe when I run into trouble. It always gets the job done. It was quite handy when I took the decklid torsion bars off. ||||reg||1
