Z||000006||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-27-2001||09:59 AM||||I had the bushing replacing on mine 3 years ago..just replaced the pivot bolt last week.. they take a lot of work to get loose, even after only sitting 3 years..   Keep the oil to it and be persistant  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||06-27-2001||03:10 PM||||Yep, bolt came out without any problems. Actually, I am working on the drivers side, and I found it more convient for me to turn the bolt and hold the nut. First thing I did was check to make sure the bolt was not stuck in the sleeve, and it wasn't, Thank god. However, this lower control arm does look fairly new, perhaps replaced by the last owner maybe. So, I hope the passenger side isn't stuck or anything, then I'd be screwed, literally.||||reg||1
Z||000008||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-27-2001||04:10 PM||||word of advice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>when you put the control arms back on.. TORQUE them correctly!   Garage that replaced mine..DIDNT..  It wore out the bushings in a  month! <P>Uppers are set to 65 Pounds. Not sure about lowers, will look it up if you want.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Leadfoot||06-27-2001||04:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>Well, 6 hours and 4 wrenchs later, I still don't have the control arm off. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Sounds about right if you ask me.  I redid my whole suspension with Prothane bushings (including the cradle).  When all was said and done it took me 72 hours.  The best way I found to take off those stubborn bolts was to use a torch and a razor sharp chisel.<BR>||||reg||1
